{"uid":"modules/lazy_world_diff.py","name":"lazy_world_diff.py","qualname":"modules/lazy_world_diff.py","kind":"module","file":"modules/lazy_world_diff.py","line":1,"end_line":636,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"World-surface diff: host snapshots, change detection, ghost liveness.","description":"The world model stores the *current* campaign truth; this module stores\nwhat a host looked like last time we looked and reports the difference:\n\n- ``host_snapshot`` reads one host out of a world-model dict as a plain,\n  canonical snapshot (open services only).\n- ``snapshot_fingerprint`` hashes a snapshot so an unchanged host never\n  re-triggers.\n- ``diff_snapshots`` returns the deterministic change list between two\n  snapshots. A product appearing where there was none is nmap\n  enrichment, not a change; a flip of an existing identity is.\n- Changes append to ``sessions/lazy_changes.jsonl`` (bounded per host,\n  prunable) so the report and the loop can read *what moved*.\n- Ghost liveness: a host whose name no longer resolves but whose last\n  known address still answers is recorded in ``sessions/lazy_ghosts.json``\n  so the operator sees the asset is not gone, only unnamed. The probe is\n  injectable and every check is read-only.\n- ``snapshot_engagement`` appends a daily point-in-time campaign snapshot\n  to ``sessions/lazy_stats_history.jsonl``.\n\nStdlib only. Every entry point degrades silently on missing data and\nnever raises on untrusted input.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["modules/lazy_world_diff.py::BASE_DIR","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::CHANGES_FILENAME","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::SNAPSHOTS_FILENAME","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::GHOSTS_FILENAME","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::STATS_FILENAME","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::HOST_NEW","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::HOST_RETURNED","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::HOST_RETIRED","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::PORT_OPENED","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::PORT_CLOSED","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::SERVICE_CHANGED","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::OS_CHANGED","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::GHOST_ENDPOINT_LIMIT","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::SurfaceChange","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::host_snapshot","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::snapshot_fingerprint","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::diff_snapshots","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::record_changes","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::recent_changes","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::prune_changes","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::load_host_snapshots","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::save_host_snapshots","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::campaign_snapshots","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::ghost_endpoints","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::name_resolves","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::load_ghosts","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::ghost_state_apply","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::find_ghost_hosts","modules/lazy_world_diff.py::snapshot_engagement"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
